combined sign through the first prime-active window ending at $R=3$
@connesconsani2023cycles. Their computation supports
$S_(2,3)>=0$ but does not prove the continuum conditional-energy
inequality. The present reduction identifies what that numerical restoration
is measuring: not an independently positive prime term, but closure of the
conditioned old--new short.

== Positivity already crosses the first prime seam

#object-entry(elements.prime_active_positivity_continuation)

This is a genuine advance over the former all-or-nothing phrasing.  If
$a=(log R)/2$, the published strict base gap gives
$lambda(a_2)>0$ at $a_2=(log 2)/2$, and Suzuki proves continuity of the
