Continuity does not provide the size of $delta$.  The first-cell obligation
is therefore quantitative rather than existential: bound the
source-derived effective tension, or equivalently control the modulus of
$lambda(a)$, all the way across
$
  [(log 2)/2,(log 3)/2].
$
If positivity first fails at some later aperture, the effective tension has
a nonzero null mode there.  This is the exact zero-tension standing mode
which the tension intuition was approaching.

