  =
  integral_0^a h_omega(x y)f(y)dif y.
$
The exact proof equivalence is
$
  "RH"
  quad arrow.l.r quad
  I+epsilon bold(H)_(omega,a)>=0
  quad
  "for every "
  omega>0,\ a>0,\ epsilon=plus.minus 1.
  quad "(BIPOLAR SOURCE LAW)"
$

This does more than rename the connected Gram requirement.  For fixed
$omega$, the source begins at exact rest:
$
  bold(H)_(omega,a)=0
  quad "when "a<=1.
$
It is locally finite in $a$, and the integer $n$ enters precisely when
$a^2$ crosses $n$, with half-density weight
$
  frac(c_omega(n),sqrt(n))
  =
  n^(omega-1/2)
  product_(p divides n)(1-p^(-2omega)).
  quad "(INTEGER CELL)"
$
This is the requested causal counting topology.  A prime axis, a repeated
prime traversal, and a composite are distinct cells, while multiplicativity
records their exact common construction.

If the cut at $b$ is split into its old interval $(0,a)$ and new shell
$(a,b)$,
