right-shift isometry.  Every new integer response is born as a triangle at
the exposed boundary and grows from there.  Thus neither the receiver nor a
prime cell is created from a blank state.

The same identity supplies a lossless boundary-port balance for each
polarity.  Interior right-shift is pure transport; only the incoming and
outgoing boundary amplitudes can alter the standing energy.  This turns the
remaining RH obligation into simultaneous causal passivity of the two port
relations.  It does not assume the old positive body in order to manufacture
