=== An isolated crossing layer cannot be the executor

#object-entry(elements.theta_crossing_layer_indefiniteness)

The obstruction is causal rather than cosmetic.  At a fixed $y$, opposed
receivers $s$ and $-s$ with $s>y$ already see each other, while neither
diagonal receiver has yet entered the layer.  The local matrix is therefore
$
  mat(0,k;k,0),
$
with one positive and one negative orientation.  Later $y$-layers introduce
the missing diagonal storage.  Consequently the source executor cannot be
memoryless in the sweep parameter: it must retain the open crossing and let
later incidence close or foil it.

On the stronger ambient coordinate face, the first accumulated bipolar law
is
$
  S(s)-C(s)>=0,
$
where $S$ is the diagonal theta tail and $C$ is the opposed crossing
integral defined in the lemma.  This is not substituted for the
RH-equivalent exponential-span condition.  It identifies exactly what the
full-coordinate Weyl route would have to transport rather than assuming each
layer was already a Gram square.

#object-entry(elements.theta_parity_execution_reduction)

The complete full-line source makes the relative law exact.  Simultaneous
sign reversal is an actual symmetry of $cal(P)_0$, so the receiver separates
into even and odd currents.  The same-hand kernel $A$ supplies storage; the
opposed-hand kernel $B$ supplies the crossing.  Neither $B>=0$ nor
layer-by-layer positivity is required.  The exact requirement is
$
  B=A^(1/2)T A^(1/2),
  quad norm(T)<=1,
$
which says that both polarities of the crossing fit within the same stored
current.  The two emitted residuals are then
$
  cal(R)_plus.minus
  =
  (1 plus.minus T)^(1/2)A^(1/2).
$

The exact Volterra reduction in @freedman2026weyl has the causal form forced
by this obstruction.  Each positive-side theta mode first factors through
the common second-order law
$
