- logarithmic lift and exponential return;
- Gaussian width $u$ and Fourier reciprocal $u arrow.r -u$;
- Poisson summation and Mellin transport;
- completed involution $J$;
- Euler-place admission $S arrow.r S union {p}$; and
- support-aperture inclusion $R arrow.r R'$.

For every generator, name its domain, target fiber, anchor into the classical
test space, adjoint, response defect, and composition law. Then compute the
